@* NotFoundPage: the answer for an address that no page handles, at "/not-found" (part of the App unit).

   The server re-executes a request that ended in 404 against this route (see ServerHost), and the Router shows it
   for an address that does not match a page inside an open session. Like every page it is rendered inside
   MainLayout, so the header and the footer are there, and it is open to everyone. The 404 status of the original
   request is kept by the re-execution. *@
@page "/not-found"

<PageTitle>Page not found - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<main class="page narrow" data-testid="not-found">
    <h1>Page not found</h1>
    <p>The address you asked for does not match any page. It may have been mistyped or the page may have moved.</p>
    <p><a class="action outline" href="/projects" data-testid="not-found-projects-link">Back to projects</a></p>
</main>
